    // --- TAB 6: HOW TO USE ---
    howtouse_title: { en: 'Usage Guide: Bitcoin Weather' },
    howtouse_intro: { en: 'The <strong>BTC Weather Panel</strong> translates complex on-chain and market indicators into a simple weather forecast, enabling fast and assertive decisions for your Bitcoin operations.' },
    howtouse_seasons: { en: 'Understand the Seasons' },
    howtouse_seasons_list: { en: '<li>☀️ <strong>Sunny (Uptrend):</strong> Dominant buying strength. LONG positions active.</li><li>��️ <strong>Cloudy (Sideways):</strong> Low volatility. Perfect for slow accumulation via DCA.</li><li>⛈️ <strong>Storm (Downtrend):</strong> Intense selling pressure. SHORT positions active.</li>' },
    howtouse_thermometer: { en: 'General Thermometer' },
    howtouse_thermometer_desc: { en: 'Consolidates 6 essential metrics into a score from <strong>-2.00 (Strong Buy)</strong> to <strong>+2.00 (Strong Sell)</strong> to guide your capital allocation and the decision banner in 1 second.' },
    howtouse_ai_title: { en: 'Artificial Intelligence Indicators' },
    howtouse_ai_indicators: { en: '<div><span style="color: var(--color-sunny); font-weight: 700;">1. Fear &amp; Greed Index (Sentiment):</span><span style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Measures retail sentiment (volatility, volume, social media). Extreme fear (&lt;25) indicates cyclical bottoms (buy); extreme greed (&gt;75) signals euphoric tops (sell).</span></div><div><span style="color: var(--color-sunny); font-weight: 700;">2. MVRV Ratio (Network Value):</span><span style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Compares market capitalization to realized capitalization. Values below 1.00 point to strong historical undervaluation; values above 3.00 indicate a price bubble.</span></div><div><span style="color: var(--color-sunny); font-weight: 700;">3. 200-Week Moving Average (200W MA):</span><span style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Cyclical long-term support average. Buying BTC near or below this average offers excellent historical return asymmetry.</span></div><div><span style="color: var(--color-sunny); font-weight: 700;">4. Monthly RSI (Relative Strength):</span><span style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Tracks macro market exhaustion. Extreme oversold values (&lt;30) indicate final capitulation, while extreme overbought (&gt;80) precedes hard corrections.</span></div><div><span style="color: var(--color-sunny); font-weight: 700;">5. Realized Price:</span><span style="color: var(--text-secondary);">The weighted average cost price of the entire network on the blockchain. Works as a critical cyclical support where few investors are in profit.</span></div><div><span style="color: var(--color-sunny); font-weight: 700;">6. Supply in Profit (% of Coins):</span><span style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Percentage of coins whose last movement occurred below the current price. Below 45% represents capitulation zones (buy); above 95% indicates cycle tops.</span></div><div><span style="color: var(--color-sunny); font-weight: 700;">7. Binance Trend (RSI + EMA 9/21 Crossover):</span><span style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Maps the local strength and direction of each timeframe (15M, 1H, 4H, etc.). The EMA 9 crossing above EMA 21 confirms buying strength (LONG); crossing below confirms selling strength (SHORT).</span></div>' },
